:[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T01:34:03-07:00","id":1096653,"title":"","content":"I got Homewreker who has terminate as a totem on the third click.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T06:42:00-07:00","id":1096702,"title":"","content":"This is rad; got a usable Lunar on 3rd try; Centor Harvester, a Hummingbird Totem Treasurehunter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T08:10:36-07:00","id":1096725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096585#post1096585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may have some totems and roles that don't quite work. For the latter, chimera isn't really a thing that informs a role, so much as what your totemic form is going to look like (which will be some combination of animals). For totems... who's the joker who put the pixiu in the list and not have it tied to being noted as a chimera? (^VVVVVV^)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually do think of &quot;Chimera&quot; as a role - it's for those Lunars who have spent so much time in the Wyld sans tattoos that their minds are gone and their bodies are a horrible mess. They're more monster than character. Not sure if this is the way it will be in 3rd edition, so I might go make some alterations as we get closer to that book coming out.<br /> <br /> I do want to encourage people to mix-and-match as needed, though. If you really like two things about a character and not the third, just swap it out with the next character in the list. Some of the humorous combos are intentional - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar298_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"298\" data-vbnamecard=\"298\">Jen</a> found the termite home-wrecker, and there's a honey badger named Invicta the Uncaring - so don't feel like you need to stick with the joke if you need a more serious character.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> <b>It's like a DAIKLAIVE made out of BICEPS!!!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T08:32:31-07:00","id":1096737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096725#post1096725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually do think of &quot;Chimera&quot; as a role - it's for those Lunars who have spent so much time in the Wyld sans tattoos that their minds are gone and their bodies are a horrible mess. They're more monster than character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently this is not how it's going to work anymore. Chimeras are lunars who specifically choose to break their caste and live outside of them. At least that's my read on what we've got so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T09:26:38-07:00","id":1096767,"title":"","content":"Is it break their caste? Or is it, as in 1st ed, mucking about with their totem? Changing their totem, which causes the new one to be warped?<br /> I'm not sure they've given a lot of detail.<br /> <br /> Because that's what I'm hoping for. I had a Lunar character with a lot of self-hate issues, and he was obsessed with changing himself. Sacrificed his own silver tattoos for sorcery, picked up (and later got rid of) various mutations. He was thinking about changing his totem. I'm hoping that's something you can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T11:41:25-07:00","id":1096801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096767#post1096767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it break their caste? Or is it, as in 1st ed, mucking about with their totem? Changing their totem, which causes the new one to be warped?<br /> I'm not sure they've given a lot of detail.<br /> <br /> Because that's what I'm hoping for. I had a Lunar character with a lot of self-hate issues, and he was obsessed with changing himself. Sacrificed his own silver tattoos for sorcery, picked up (and later got rid of) various mutations. He was thinking about changing his totem. I'm hoping that's something you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we'll have to wait until lunars drops to get a definitive answer, but until then either way could work. So long as it's the lunars showing agency rather than some sort of magical cancer that only they can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[