:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T11:52:30-07:00","id":1096806,"title":"","content":"I think that I wouldn't make any assumptions about that absent more information, and that i don't think insane is a meaningful word here.<br /> <br /> He definitely sounds depressed though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T12:09:37-07:00","id":1096822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096803#post1096803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars broke their Castes and don't have one unless they get their Moonsilver tattoos.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, Chimeras are just the ones who don't get the Moonsilver Tattoos, maybe because they don't want to or they avoid the Silver Pact. Whatever benefits they gain from being Casteless, it does joy involve the Wyld in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't what chimerae are going to be anymore, per word from back when EX3 was announced. They're just Lunars who alter their spirit shape to have features and parts of other animals. Unlike in first edition, there is no penalty for this (it formerly involved buying Finding the Spirit's Shape again, paying a dot of Willpower, and getting on an animal avatar's shit list, or something of that sort). So you can still be one, even with tattoos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T12:15:55-07:00","id":1096824,"title":"","content":"Could you source that please? I'm interested in hearing more about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T12:35:19-07:00","id":1096829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096824#post1096824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you source that please? I'm interested in hearing more about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>, mostly in the beginning and then in slightly greater detail a bit further down. While those were preliminary takes that we've been told are subject to change, we can be fairly sure that there won't be any Wyld-monster Lunars in EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T13:07:51-07:00","id":1096838,"title":"","content":"Oh wow I just noticed my post didn't make it clear that I was saying whatever the Chimera are, it doesn't involve the Wyld this time around. Thanks for the link anywho!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T14:03:06-07:00","id":1096858,"title":"","content":"Do the Lunars run like KENYANS!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T14:26:04-07:00","id":1096865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096805#post1096805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it just occurred to me that this makes Ma-Ha-Suchi even more insane than he already was portrayed. He chose to turn away from his ultra-sexy first age Casanova persona and live as a goat-wolf his own damn self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I've always been a paragon regarding discussing mental illness, but considering May is Mental Health Month, I thought I'd mayhaps ask you to take a second and clarify your position, because right now it looks like you're taking this into bad territory.<br /> <br /> (Also if Rutting Pens Ma-Ha-Suchi isn't canon anymore, surely his Meat Loaf-pun DotFA write-up with its Motivation of seducing every Celestial Exalt isn't either\u2026?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-25-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T14:43:40-07:00","id":1096872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096865#post1096865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I've always been a paragon regarding discussing mental illness, but considering May is Mental Health Month, I thought I'd mayhaps ask you to take a second and clarify your position, because right now it looks like you're taking this into bad territory.<br /> <br /> (Also if Rutting Pens Ma-Ha-Suchi isn't canon anymore, surely his DotFA Motivation of wanting to seduce every Celestial Exalt isn't either\u2026?)</div> </div> </div> </div>My position is that the portrayal of Ma-Ha-Suchi in 2E was of a seriously mentally disturbed individual. <br /> <br /> Since The nameless lair of Ma-Ha-Suchi is still on the 3E map I assume they're still bringing him in. However given what they're changing with lunars he can no longer be explained as a product of wyld taint, so if they still plan on portraying him as a goat-wolf murder monster kinda guy there's likely gonna be a big component of mental health issues that's he's laboring under. <br /> <br /> I was unaware of the rutting pens being removed in this edition. I am not sorry to see them go. That and stuff from infernals were some of the biggest turn offs in 2E from my perspective. As far as his first age persona, I don't think we have any info one way or another, but why would they chuck that? Falls from grace stories are huge. Plus the beauty destroyed idea is a big one. Although in this case it would be the beast destroying his own beauty and turning away from what he once was. Handled <i>properly</i> you could have a very compelling story of loss and thirst for revenge that doesn't even include <b>one </b>horrible rape pit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T14:56:15-07:00","id":1096875,"title":"","content":"Again, his DotFA writeup was for the sake of a Meat Loaf reference. <i>Meat Loaf</i>.<br /> <br /> And given the devs' position on inclusivity I would hope they'd handle the issue of mental health with more sensitivity than you're suggesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-25-2017, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T14:59:22-07:00","id":1096876,"title":"","content":"It might be worthwhile to actually consult the write up for the Nameless Lair in the Third Edition book. Because it's there, on page 109.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T20:02:11-07:00","id":1096959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096725#post1096725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually do think of &quot;Chimera&quot; as a role - it's for those Lunars who have spent so much time in the Wyld sans tattoos that their minds are gone and their bodies are a horrible mess. They're more monster than character. Not sure if this is the way it will be in 3rd edition, so I might go make some alterations as we get closer to that book coming out.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096737#post1096737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently this is not how it's going to work anymore. Chimeras are lunars who specifically choose to break their caste and live outside of them. At least that's my read on what we've got so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096767#post1096767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it break their caste? Or is it, as in 1st ed, mucking about with their totem? Changing their totem, which causes the new one to be warped?<br /> I'm not sure they've given a lot of detail.<br /> <br /> Because that's what I'm hoping for. I had a Lunar character with a lot of self-hate issues, and he was obsessed with changing himself. Sacrificed his own silver tattoos for sorcery, picked up (and later got rid of) various mutations. He was thinking about changing his totem. I'm hoping that's something you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1096803#post1096803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars broke their Castes and don't have one unless they get their Moonsilver tattoos.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, Chimeras are just the ones who don't get the Moonsilver Tattoos, maybe because they don't want to or they avoid the Silver Pact. Whatever benefits they gain from being Casteless, it does not involve the Wyld in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Y'all might be interested in what Robert Vance had to say in the Ask The Devs thread.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1096841#post1096841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are chimerae just Lunars who have stacked two or more animals into their spirit shape/DBT form? If so, is there a taboo to it? Are horrific Wyld Mutant Lunars still a thing separately from Chimerae?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1096848#post1096848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently envisioning &quot;chimerism&quot; as a cascade of Charms that follow from warping your spirit shape.<br /> <br /> I doubt there will be [a taboo to it].<br /> <br /> Moonsilver tattoos let the Lunars traverse the Wyld as easily as they can survive in any of Creation's harsh climes. If there's going to be a horrific mutant Exalt, it seems like they most likely be anything <i>but </i>a Lunar. That doesn't mean you can't have them in the game, but bodes poorly for them being a Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1096856#post1096856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the tattoos weren't a reaction to a &quot;problem&quot; as in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1096857#post1096857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tattoos were created as part of the Lunars' undertaking of breaking and remaking their Castes.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1096879#post1096879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Shapeshifting have Charm cascades separate from the Attribute trees to govern stuff like what forms you can change into and for stuff like your spirit shape, or will those be integrated into the main Attribute trees?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1096888#post1096888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrated into their Attribute Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Lunar Exalted are the LEAST likely Exalted to mutate uncontrollably into mindless monsters. (Which makes sense -- they are supposed to be the Exalted who most exemplify controlled and temporary transformations.)<br /> <br /> 2) Moonsilver Tattoos are primarily intended to fix a Lunar's Caste into one of the new three forms. They protect against the Wyld but are not primarily intended for such a function, and they apparently have nothing to do with chimerism.<br /> <br /> 3) Chimerism is a deliberate choice which could be represented with a special branch of Charms.<br /> <br /> 4) On that note, shapeshifting Charms are just Charms again, not separated Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T20:20:43-07:00","id":1096964,"title":"","content":"I will admit I liked 2E Chimerae as a horrific perversion to Lunars the way Abyssals are to Solars, but I'm totally cool with &quot;Wyld-taint&quot; not being a default part of the Lunar condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T02:15:22-07:00","id":1097051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder quoting Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm currently envisioning &quot;chimerism&quot; as a cascade of Charms that follow from warping your spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I actually missed that.<br /> <br /> That's basically exactly what I'd like to see. My Lunar PC retired (because he got amnesia from his rampant mutating-without-tattoos, and so was sent off to the Silver Pact to learn about being a Lunar... which as an Essence 4, 700xp Lunar he probably should have a long time ago, but who was going to make him? He had stuff to do), but when the Lunar book comes out I might bring him back, and those are exactly the sort of charms I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wondered if, since there are a whole bunch of new Exalt types being planned, if one of them might have the &quot;mutate into a gribbly monster-spawn-thing&quot; vibe going on, with it being taken away from Lunars. The Protean stuff people always go on about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:47:30-07:00","id":1097230,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a>: Thanks for the info. I don't often have time to read through the Ask the Devs thread (though I super-appreciate that it's there), and it's not collated anywhere that I'm aware of, so I miss a lot of these things.<br /> <br /> I've swapped &quot;Chimera&quot; out of the &quot;Role&quot; section in favor of a more general &quot;Monster&quot; description. If it becomes appropriate to add chimerism back into the tables I'll do so then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:23:18-07:00","id":1097264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1097230#post1097230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..and it's not collated anywhere that I'm aware of, so I miss a lot of these things</div> </div> </div> </div>There actually is a rolling google doc somewhere that's collecting the answers, but damned if I can find the link.<br /> <br /> Another place is <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/10319\" target=\"_blank\">Ask the Dev's compilation on Nishkriya</a>, but it's obviously not sorted as nicely as that google doc. Hopefully someone can find that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe