97270#post1097270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, does it count as stealing the spotlight if this was already a thread about Lunars, just on a different topic?<br /> <br /> \u200bBut the original topic doesn't exactly sustain much conversation, so is a wide tangent kind of a necessity?<br /> <br /> I'm so confused!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the natural tendency of Lunar threads. Nothing to see here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:25:28-07:00","id":1097321,"title":"","content":"I'm sorely tempted to make MHS a solid straight up (misunderstood) good guy this time around, both to amuse myself and throw my players a curveball from way out of left field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13245-eminent-professor","name":"Eminent Professor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13245_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T20:04:04-07:00","id":1097397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eminent Professor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1097321#post1097321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorely tempted to make MHS a solid straight up (misunderstood) good guy this time around, both to amuse myself and throw my players a curveball from way out of left field.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a GM pull off Good Guy <i>Raksi</i>, so, it's not impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T16:08:09-07:00","id":1097631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1097278#post1097278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the natural tendency of Lunar threads. Nothing to see here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's ok, the more people hijack this thread the more people see my Lunar Generator. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Honestly, I should put links to my blog and my other interactives at the bottom of that page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T17:17:00-07:00","id":1097640,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit conflicted about the idea of creating a cascade of Charms based on incorporating a major transformation of one's character and bound to a specific form of spirit shape. It feels a lot more drastic than things like Attribute or Ability minimums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T01:40:51-07:00","id":1097712,"title":"","content":"It is more drastic, yes? I don't really see that as a problem. I mean, if it was like 30 charms, sure, but surely it's okay to have 4 or 5 charms that require something more drastic than attribute and ability mins.<br /> Of course, I don't see it as drastic, so much as radical. And radical is cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:25:09-07:00","id":1097727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1097712#post1097712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if it was like 30 charms, sure, but surely it's okay to have 4 or 5 charms that require something more drastic than attribute and ability mins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. And if they're a collection of Charms that are mostly focused on expansions on the already existing chimera concept, that wouldn't be so bad.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would just have concerns over some possibly interesting and useful powers being something that the central Lunar concept is hard locked out of.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, I don't see it as drastic, so much as radical. And radical is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPardon?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T10:11:19-07:00","id":1097810,"title":"","content":"What I mean is, I'm quite happy to have a Lunar that has some drastically altered powers, and I'm quite happy for those to require more than just Strength 4, Essence 2.<br /> I enjoyed playing a casteless Lunar with plenty of permanent (well, semi-permanent after a bit of wyld-questing and/or my special combo) bizarre mutations a lot in 2nd ed. I don't want to be told &quot;this Chimerae stuff seems a bit too radically odd, a bit too drastic, maybe a bit harmful to the character, so, you can't take it.&quot; Sometimes I got that impression with people talking about 2nd ed; &quot;oh, being a Chimarae is so awful, these mutation rules are really harsh, it's terrible to poor Lunars&quot; but I loved playing it. I had a 700xp casteless Lunar. I mean, sure, I don't see a need to force others to play a character I liked when they didn't (by saying that all Lunars inevitably if slowly become gribbly tentacle monsters without tattoos), but what I mean is, I don't want the writers going &quot;oh, Chimarae seem like a sub-optimal choice, so we'll clean them up.&quot; I don't want them to be made mainstream! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I want to be able to say &quot;Yes, my character is warping his own Owl totem and unlocking forbidden powers that touch the edge of what shapeshifting is&quot;. Not force people to do it, sure, that's fine, but I want the option if I want to.<br /> <br /> I do see your point about<b></b>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">some possibly interesting and useful powers being something that the central Lunar concept is hard locked out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>but I think the answer is simply (like most charms), that they ought to have powers that are thematic to being a chimerae. So these shouldn't be powers that are appropriate to regular Lunars anyway. I don't think that there'd be many powers that are thematic to chimerae and not regular Lunars; but out of a few hundred Lunar charms, I'm sure the writers can think of 5-10 that are appropriate for Chimerae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T10:51:04-07:00","id":1097823,"title":"","content":"There are some things there that I wasn't even thinking about. The problems with the Second Edition thing is a whole other conversation, that... maybe another time.<br /> <br /> \u200bAll I was thinking about were the issues of having a set of powers so tied into a particular character aesthetic. I'm trying to think of something analogous, tasteful or otherwise, but it doesn't really track because it's a premise that is so distinct to Lunars that most other things I could think of feel ludicrous.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose I could make a point by staying within Lunars though. For instance, imagine if there were Charm cascades that you were locked out of entirely because your spirit shape was above a certain size; would there not be a problem with that? In terms of things like the pressure it might create at character creation, and the long term constraints it would create?<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think the potential to be able to become a chimera in play necessarily helps this, because I feel as though the Lunar premise is one in which it's reasonable for a lot of people to be attached to their totem choices, and it would be pointlessly unfair to create a sense of punishing people for that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI was assuming as a matter of course that whatever Charms chimera get are still appropriate Lunar Charms that won't wade back into that quagmire of rendering them thematically and cosmetically incoherent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T16:22:34-07:00","id":1097899,"title":"","content":"Well, being a Chimerae isn't something you start out as like being a tyrant-lizard totem Lunar is; it's something you become.<br /> Presumably, in 3rd ed, by taking the &quot;You are now a Chimerae&quot; charm.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it's not a seperate choice to the charm cascade; it is the charm cascade (I'm guessing/suggesting). So, it's not so different from taking your sorcerous initiation and spells, say. It's just another option. One that is cosmetically (and thematically) distinct, but not mechanically (I mean, more than any other charm tree).<br /> <br /> Which, I realise may now sound like me going back to what you said earlier about how they should be attributes and abilities and not much else; so, in the mechanical sense, yes. The prerequisites for &quot;Ultimate Chimerae Gribbly Mutant Ascension&quot; might just be &quot;Stamina 3, Essence 4, Finding the Spirit's Shape&quot; or whatever.<br /> But that first charm is the charm that says &quot;you are now a Chimerae, pick a new totem&quot; as it did in 1st ed.<br /> (Or whatever; not saying it has to work precisely like that, but I think you should be able to understand what I'm getting at; it's not that you become a Chimerae and thus can access the special super-gated Chimerae charms, like in 2nd ed; but rather, you become a Chimerae by taking the Chimerae charms, just as you become a Lunar able to turn into a giant monster by taking the giant monster charms, or you become a Lunar prophet by taking Eagle-and-Fish Prophecy, or you become a super-strong Lunar by taking the super-strong-dude charm tree)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:12:45-07:00","id":1097906,"title":"","content":"A Chimera branch is the perfect place to reuse names like Hybrid Body Rearrangement, Perfected Hybrid Interaction, and Terrifying Beastman Alteration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T01:40:09-07:00","id":1098025,"title":"","content":"I agree. Perfected Hybrid Interaction was always a knack that I felt was only in-theme for Chimerae anyway.<br /> My casteless Lunar turned into a giant stone-skinned, clawed monster (like a gargoyle but without wings). Cool, but is that in theme for regular Lunars? I don't think so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T02:44:17-07:00","id":1098041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096562-so-many-lunars-400-lunars?p=1097899#post1097899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not that you become a Chimerae and thus can access the special super-gated Chimerae charms, like in 2nd ed; but rather, you become a Chimerae by taking the Chimerae charms</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that the sole function of chimera Charms would be to characterise oneself as a chimera would be better, sure. If they entail such a transformation, then the best case scenario is one in which people who like their spirit shape the way it is aren't missing out on anything, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">just as you become a Lunar able to turn into a giant monster by taking the giant monster charms, or you become a Lunar prophet by taking Eagle-and-Fish Prophecy, or you become a super-strong Lunar by taking the super-strong-dude charm tree)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThose aren't equivalent, because they don't entail something like a permanent, somewhat intrusive cosmetic change to the character.<br /> <br /> \u200bTheir functions are also a lot more apparent.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose that does lead back around to the question of why one should want to be a chimera in the first place. It's my understanding that in First Edition, it represented a kind of failure state; one had attempted to change their spirit shape from one to another, and got stuck in between. It's just that somewhere along the way, the in-between state became desirable in its own right.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich might fold back into the concern I have about chimera Charms. Charms that branch away from the state feel like they're at least flirting with the idea of chimerism being a special form of Lunar superpower, which I think sells the default Lunar concept a bit short. But if it <i>didn't</i> have much in the way of extra powers, it would raise the question of why one would want to add wolf features to their goat totem in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf it was all a purely cosmetic thing, then I would think it would be a lot less circuitous to let mutant animals be a possible spirit shape from the start.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut when it gets given a particular name, it lends it the assumption of a bit of weight and significance, and I alternately see a struggle to live up to that assumption and issues that arise should there be actual success.<br /> <br /> \u200bI remember ages ago, there was developer discussion about the idea of spirit shape having a possible impact on how one learned Lunar Charms in general; nothing as dividing as &quot;Lunar with snake totem can only learn snake Charms&quot;, more a case that the totem created a theme that could change some of the progression of a cascade to make accessing some things easier. In that model, I would have thought that the benefit of a hybridized spirit shape was being able to expand into such rearrangement following two or more animal themes, while giving up the highest benefits of having a singular totem. I feel as though that would have been a decent way to give chimerism a point, without handing it something exclusive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}